# Causal soundness, identification completeness and native finite models

This facade reexports the semantic theorems and applications. Detailed
hypotheses and proof explanations remain in the named implementation modules.

## Soundness and the positive-class converse

`Certificates` and `Correspondence` define the certificate shapes and the
`PublishedSoundness` / `PublishedCompleteness` records.
`Soundness` constructs `ObservedGraph.publishedSoundness`: supported
do-calculus derivations preserve interpreted causal values in compatible
finite models. Its partition proofs use the actual graph mutilations and
separation predicates defined by the causal foundations.

`KernelSuccessCompilation` and `ConditionalCompilation` certify the literal
joint-ID and IDC outputs. `KernelFailureExtraction` and
`ConditionalFailureCore` recover original-query failure data;
`ConditionalFailureCarrierCases` is a separately qualified carrier constructor.
`HedgeChannelCounterexample` and `ConditionalFailureTerminalCounterexample`
construct positive countermodels; their cores do not assume success
soundness. `HedgeChannelCompleteness` assembles
`ObservedGraph.publishedCompleteness` for the full positive class on
value-rich finite observed signatures. Restricted hedge constructions remain
useful local results with their geometric hypotheses stated at their owners.

## Original hidden DAGs and supported zeros

`InterventionalEntropy` reads the existing observational and interventional
assignment records as Shannon laws and proves that agreement of an entire
law identifies its entropy. `EntropyAssessment` records which entropy
projects are useful here: Shannon inequalities as sound exclusion tests,
not a Bayesian graph posterior, Körner graph entropy, or loopy entropy
message passing. `GraphQueryUncertainty` is a finite catalogue of Markov
hypotheses given data; it is not a graph posterior and is not a substitute
for ID/IDC. `ShannonElimination` attempts Fourier–Motzkin hidden-variable
elimination of elemental Shannon inequalities; it is sound and incomplete.

`HiddenDAGCollapse`, `HiddenDAGProbability` and `HiddenDAGCountermodelLift`
connect projected constructions to actual original finite hidden-DAG records.
`HiddenDAGCorrespondence` packages native positive-class joint and conditional
identification equivalences, allowing arbitrary finite hidden/private-noise
alphabets and retaining the observed value-richness premise.

`GuardedPrintedSoundness` and `GuardedAdmissibleCertificates` construct and
interpret support-qualified literal-output certificates in models containing
zeros. `HiddenDAGSupportedDomain` specifies the semantic application domain
independently of engine success; `HiddenDAGSupportedCorrespondence` supplies
its joint, conditional and hedge completeness package. The actually used
conditionals and original conditional target's support remain explicit.

`FiniteSource` provides executable finite-table semantics and its preservation
bridge. `PositiveModal`, `SupportedModal`, `ModalRealization` and the modal
and counterfactual transports connect certificates to actual mode-theory
executions.

## Representation, bounds and checked formula families

The `HiddenDAG*Representation` and `ProjectionTemplateRepresentation`
constructions give finite structural representatives preserving the whole
observed law and the stated finite target family. Structural cardinality
bounds and rational denominator bounds are separate parameters.

`BinaryBowBounds`, `BinaryBowAttainable` and `BinaryInstrumental.Attainable`
expose exact bounds, identification and attainable-set results. The
instrumental-variable family includes null instrument arms, both treatment
risks and the signed average treatment effect.
`SharedResponseLinearBounds` supplies unrestricted-denominator attained
unconditional event bounds in the complete-bidirected native class;
`SharedResponseSupportedSolver` is its separate support-filtered adapter.

`BoundedNativeClassification` and its conditional inspection/search companions
classify their declared bounded native families.
`NativeCertificateCheck`, `NativeFormulaSelection` and observational formula
catalogues retain the actual guards and conditional-support premises.
Search completeness concerns the supplied or generated finite family.
`HiddenDAGPolynomialEvidence` checks supplied polynomial bound certificates
for the stated structural templates.

`Thesis.AxiomAudit` is the collection gate for prefix axiom audits and the
removed-identification name check. The permitted transitive kernel axioms
are `propext` and `Quot.sound`.
-/
